WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.837
Use this checkpoint to connect requirements with objects.

00:00:02.837 --> 00:00:05.442
Temporary stages suggest a CTE.

00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:08.847
Shared live relational logic suggests a standard view.

00:00:08.847 --> 00:00:13.517
An expensive summary with acceptable refresh delay suggests a materialized view.

00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:18.242
A controlled filtered one-table interface may use an updatable view and check option.

00:00:18.242 --> 00:00:21.052
The object choice should follow the contract you need.

00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:24.532
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:24.532 --> 00:00:28.957
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:28.957 --> 00:00:31.972
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:31.972 --> 00:00:35.722
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:35.722 --> 00:00:41.722
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:41.722 --> 00:00:45.307
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:45.307 --> 00:00:49.073
not only whether the statement executes.
